<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n49266" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θῠγάτηρ</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ], ἡ</span>, gen. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγᾰτέρος</span>
		
			contr.
		
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγατρός</span>; dat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγᾰτέρι, θυγατρί</span>; acc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγᾰτέρα</span>
		
			Ep.
		
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύγατρα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					1.13
				</span></i>
			; voc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύγᾰτερ</span>: nom. pl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγατέρες</span>, 
				Ep.
			 and lyr. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύγατρες</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					9.144
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				20a
			</span></i>.<i><span class="en">
				16
			</span></i>: gen. pl. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τέρων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					22.832.19
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				461c
			</span></i>, poet. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τρῶν</span>: dat. pl.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τράσι</span>
			
				Ep.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τέρεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					15.197
				</span></i>
			; both sets of forms are found in poetry, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θυγατρός, -τρί, -τράσι</span> are used in
				Prose:—<i>daughter</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				9.148
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				290
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				4.4
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θύγατρες ἵππων</span>, of
			mules, <i><span class="en">
				Simon.
				7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. ταύρων</span>, of bees, Philo
			Tars. ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.269
			</span></i>: metaph., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μοισᾶν
			θυγατέρες</span>, of Odes, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>N.</u>
				4.3
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλάστιγξ ἡ χαλκοῦ θ</span>.
				<i><span class="en">
				Critias
				1.9D.
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θ. Σειληνοῦ</span>, of the vine,
				<i><span class="en">
				Jul.
				<u>Caes.</u>
				25
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψήφου συμβολικῆς θ</span>., of a
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάγυνος</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.248
			</span></i> (Marc. Arg.); of villages dependent on a city, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jd.</u>
				1.27
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>1 Ma.</u>
				5.8
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> later,
				<i>maidservant, slave</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phalar.
				<u>Ep.</u>
				142.3
			</span></i>. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῡ</span> in 
				Ep.
			 in the longer forms, metri gr.] (Cf. Skt.
				<i>duhitár-</i>, Engl. <i>daughter</i>,
		etc.)</div>
